WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.183 --> 00:00:02.670
(rockets whooshing)

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.690
- [Narrator] In the wake of Hamas's

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.720
horrific surprise attacks
in Southern Israel,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.340
the Israeli Army is preparing

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.723
for a full scale ground
assault of the Gaza Strip.

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:13.836
(rockets whooshing)

00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:15.990
(explosions booming)

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.120
On Friday, the Israeli military

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.070
demanded the people of Gaza City

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.170
move to the southern part of the enclave,

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.121
because military operations
would take place.

00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:27.360
(rockets whooshing)

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.210
- There is a term that is
often used in the military

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.760
called the center of gravity.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.030
It's a term that denotes

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.510
where all the strength of
the enemy emanates from.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.530
And obviously, in the case of Hamas,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.733
the center of gravity is inside Gaza.

00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:49.470
(explosion booms)

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.830
Israel's goals for this
operation are three.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.300
Get the hostages back,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.710
conduct a retribution for the attacks,

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.710
and to remove Hamas as
a force inside of Gaza,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.980
so that it will never be
a threat to Israel again.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.510
- [Narrator] Mark Kimmitt is a retired

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.280
US Army Brigadier General,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.160
who served in Bosnia, Kosovo, and Iraq.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.660
- It's very important to understand

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.120
how small the Gaza Strip is.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.120
Its border is 25 miles along the shore,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:28.730
and the border on land
runs for about 36 miles.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:33.360
That's twice the size of Washington DC.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.560
The challenge for the
Israeli defense forces

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.070
as they attack in is the terrain itself.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:45.870
Not only is it small, but it's
heavily populated throughout.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:50.610
There are very few open areas in Gaza,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.690
and as a result, when
you attack into Gaza,

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.970
it is not a military operation

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:01.053
with long range tanks
firing against each other.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.930
Every area of Gaza can be reached

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.920
by weapons firing in one
direction, or the other.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.220
So from the moment the
Israelis cross into Gaza,

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.380
they're in somebody's gun sights.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.770
Now, how would the Israelis attack?

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:24.420
Their goal will inevitably
be the city of Gaza.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.250
Looking at a map, you would expect them

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.430
to come primarily through the center here,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.430
to cut off the city of Gaza,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.760
as well as use this little open area

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.690
between the populated south,
and the populated north.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.430
At first glance, I would expect them

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.060
to come with their main attack into,

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.940
and as near as possible
to the city of Gaza,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.519
to try to isolate it from
the rest of the Gaza Strip.

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:54.840
(horns blaring)
(person shouts in Arabic)

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.210
- [Narrator] General Kimmitt
believes a ground invasion

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.790
could complicate the
effort to save the hostages

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.980
Hamas terrorists took into Gaza.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.980
- What is being asked for
in a full scale invasion,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.860
urban conflict, uprooting
Hamas leadership,

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:15.420
and bringing back the hostages alive,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.370
it's not something that's typically done

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.540
by a conventional army.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.940
They're not trained to do that.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.270
And if you take a look at
the terrain inside of Gaza,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.820
particularly with the
extensive tunnel system,

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.490
and the fact that Hamas
has had years and years

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.840
to prepare defenses,

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.930
a ground invasion would actually

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.020
risk the lives of those hostages more than

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.233
increase the chances of them
being brought out alive.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.180
- [Narrator] Zooming out,

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.400
General Kimmitt sees additional threats

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.990
coming from hostile forces

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.050
in Israel's neighboring
nations and territories.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.620
- Going clockwise, you
obviously have Hezbollah,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.320
which is a threat, but not a major threat.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.620
They would probably attack directly south.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.800
You've got militant groups in Syria.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.680
The typical attack route is
through the Golan Heights,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.770
or through Shebaa Farms.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.650
Obviously, you have West Bank militants,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.590
which could attack towards Tel Aviv,

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.610
but more than likely,

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.940
they will make their
focus towards Jerusalem.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.940
And even in the Sinai
Peninsula and here in Egypt,

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.040
there remain a number of
threats in the Sinai itself.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.540
Primarily, Al-Qaeda elements.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.540
Any of these organizations
could be a threat to Israel.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.060
They would be distracting attacks,

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:42.630
attempting to pull forces
away from the main battle

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.340
down here in Gaza.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.240
But now that the Israeli
forces are mobilized,

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.640
I don't believe that they
would have the capability

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.100
to be any more than a distraction,

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.160
and not have any consequence
on the operations

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.050
against Gaza City.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.580
- [Narrator] Zooming out still further,

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.950
General Kimmitt sees
additional regional threats

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.120
for the Israelis.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.330
- I think it's important to
understand the far threat,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.010
not just the near threat.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.950
The popular mobilization forces in Iraq,

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.313
some of them have pledged
fealty to this fight.

00:05:15.454 --> 00:05:18.750
And even down here in
Yemen, the Houthis in Yemen

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.690
believe it will be a multi-pronged war,

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:26.190
and we could very well
see Houthi involvement

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:29.190
on the side of Hamas in this fight.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.130
I don't necessarily
believe that they will pose

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.680
as much of a military threat

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.530
as they would pose a diplomatic threat.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:42.240
The normalization efforts
between Saudi Arabia and Israel

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.790
pretty much on the shelf.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.480
The entente that was being,

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.430
or detente that was being developed

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:55.430
between Saudi Arabia and
Iran, probably on the shelf.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.000
(people chanting)

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.130
Most important, the street,

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.310
the community of Muslims in the region.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:06.270
The ummah, the street, is active again,

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.510
and almost universally condemning Israel

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:14.284
for the attacks that they
will conduct into Gaza.

00:06:14.284 --> 00:06:15.515
(tense music)

00:06:15.515 --> 00:06:17.430
(gun fires)

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.430
I think the history of Israel since 1948

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.800
has been a series of
conflicts that, in many ways,

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.220
resemble what we're seeing here today.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.650
Perhaps not in scale, perhaps not in size,

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.600
but certainly in intent,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.110
whether it was the attempt to destroy

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:36.267
the state of Israel in 1948,

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:40.050
the '67 attacks, the '73 attacks,

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:44.970
the repeated incursions into
Gaza by the Israeli Army.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:49.170
Sadly, this is new in terms of its scale.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.860
It's new in terms of the
tactics employed by Hamas,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.690
but it is 75 years old in
terms of what Israel has faced

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:01.265
as a threat to their state since 1948.

00:07:01.265 --> 00:07:04.598
(tense music continues)

